+# The Daily Grind
+
+Static homepage (`index.html`). Serve with `pnpm start`.
+
+## Encrypted delivery notes
+
+Customers can attach private courier notes (gate codes, allergies…) on the homepage. Notes are
+encrypted **in the browser** to the shop's public key; only the sealed envelope leaves the page.
+
+| Suite | Shared secret | Notes |
+| --- | --- | --- |
+| `XWING-MLKEM768-X25519` (default) | X-Wing hybrid KEM: ML-KEM-768 + X25519 | secure if either component holds |
+| `MLKEM768` | ML-KEM-768 KEM (FIPS 203) | post-quantum only |
+| `X25519` | ephemeral-static X25519 key agreement | classical fallback |
+
+Key schedule: HKDF-SHA-256 (salt binds suite, recipient public key and encapsulation) →
+single-use AES-256-GCM key. The whole envelope header (version, suite, key id, encapsulation,
+nonce, order ref, timestamp) is authenticated as AAD; plaintext is padded to 128-byte buckets.
+
+- `js/sealed-notes.js` – crypto core (browser + Node), `js/delivery-notes.js` – homepage UI
+- `vendor/noble-pq-0.7.1.min.js` – bundled `@noble/post-quantum@0.7.1` + `@noble/curves@2.4.0` (MIT)
+- `keys/delivery-notes.json` – published public keys (fetched by the browser)
+
+```sh
+pnpm keys:generate            # new key pairs; secrets go to ~/.daily-grind/secrets (override: DG_SECRETS_DIR)
+pnpm notes:open envelope.json # decrypt one envelope or a JSON array of them
+pnpm test                     # round-trip, tamper, wrong-key and downgrade tests
+```
+
+Secret keys are written **outside** the repo because `pnpm start` serves the repo root.
+Envelopes are POSTed to `/api/delivery-notes`; that backend is not part of this static site, so
+until it exists the browser keeps the (encrypted) envelopes in `localStorage`
+(`dg.deliveryNotes.pending`) and shows them for copy/paste.
